Here are some common ones and some good ways to get them:

Poison resistance:  Cave spiders (lots of other monsters, like giant
spiders and killer bees, can give it to you, but most of these are
poisonous themselves, so eating them is not suggested unless you
already have P.R. or a unicorn horn)

Fire resistance:  Red Molds.  Or red dragons/fire giants if you
haven't been able to get it first.

Cold resistance:  Brown molds, blue gellies, or white D's/frost giants
in a worst-case scenario.

Teleport:  Nymphs, leprechauns.  Be careful with this one!

Teleport control:  Tengus.

Polymorph:  Chameleons...or were-creatures, sort of.  Be careful with
this one, too.

Disintegration resistance:  Black dragons.  Sort of a catch-22.

Sleep resistance:  Elves.  Not suggested if you're an elf (but then
you'll already have it).

Speed:  Quantum mechanics.  An odd number of times.  Speed boots make
you even faster.

Aggrivate monster:  Dogs, cats, and humans.  Not recommended.

Regeneration:  Trolls, I think, but I haven't gotten it in a while.

Some other healthy corpses:

Puddings/oozes/jellies/gelatinous cubes, if you have poison
resistance.  You can get various intrinsics.

Lizards/acid blobs:  Counteract a cockatrice's hissing.  Lizard
corpses never rot.

Wraiths:  Levels.  Getting millions of 'em via a cursed bell of
opening isn't nice, IMHO.

Giants:  Strength.  Get this from spinach and royal jelly, too.

Mind Flayers:  Intelligence.

